      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Spring storms in Utah cause roof damage primarily through heavy wet snow, high wind gusts, sudden hail impacts, and melting ice dams. These weather events lead to cracked or bruised shingles, torn flashing, granule loss, and costly indoor water leaks if left unchecked.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "heavy wet snow, high wind gusts, sudden hail impacts, and melting ice dams"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Types of Spring Roof Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "High Winds: Lift, loosen, or tear away asphalt shingles and damage metal edge flashing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hail Impact:\nBruise and fracture shingle mats, leaving dark spots or stripping protective granules into gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heavy Snow and Sleet: Strain roof decking and cause slow moisture seepage as temperatures fluctuate."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Falling Debris:\nScratch, puncture, or crack roofing materials when nearby tree branches snap."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Inspection and Warning Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check gutters and downspouts from the ground for an accumulation of loose shingle granules."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Look for missing, curling, or mismatched shingle pieces scattered in the yard\n."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect metal vents, flashing, and soft metals (like AC units or gutters) for visible dents from hail."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check attic spaces or ceilings for fresh water stains or damp insulation."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          7,
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Steps to Take"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Climbing onto a wet or damaged roof can be dangerous and cause further structural harm."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document everything:\nTake clear photographs of damaged siding, dented gutters, and any indoor leaks from the ground."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate further damage: Use buckets or temporary emergency tarps if water is actively entering the home."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Watch out for out-of-state \"storm chasers\":\nVerify that any contractor inspecting your home is licensed locally in Utah."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          5,
          6,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you would like more specific help, please tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of roof material\nyou have (asphalt shingle, tile, metal)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are seeing active leaks inside the home"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The city or area in Utah where your property is located"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for an inspection or insurance claim."
      }
